DeviceChain - dcctl bootstrap - instance acme - kind-devicechain - v1.11.0
\x1b[2m----------------------------------------------------------------------------\x1b[m
\x1b[1;34mRoot-key escrow\x1b[m

DeviceChain encrypts stored credentials with this instance's root key.
Database backups do not contain it. To recover after losing the cluster you
need this escrow file and its passphrase. Copy the file off this machine;
keep the passphrase separately.

> \x1b[7m(*) Write an encrypted escrow file (recommended)\x1b[m
  ( ) Do not escrow the root key (--no-escrow)

  \x1b[1mLocation  \x1b[m/home/op/.devicechain/escrow/acme-rootkey.escrow
            \x1b[2mdefault for this instance, on this machine, outside what 'dcctl\x1b[m
            \x1b[2mdestroy' removes\x1b[m

  Passphrase supplied by protected file (--escrow-passphrase-file). Nothing
  will be asked.

